{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the hair in the affliction.</b> This means black hair that was there before the affliction developed in it, and it turned white — it is impure, for the hair that turned white is a sign that the flesh has weakened, since the affliction kills the flesh, as it is written regarding Miriam: ״אל נא תהי כמת״ etc. And also the elderly, when they weaken, their hair turns white. But if the white hair preceded the affliction, then it is not a sign of impurity, for it did not turn white because of the affliction. And thus the Sages said: a bright spot that precedes the white hair — impure; white hair that precedes the bright spot — pure."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:35.584303446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}